    "answer": "hug/carrying-in-one's-arms-(a-baby,-pet,-doll,-etc.)",
    "mnemonic": "You know that the kanji means <kanji>hug</kanji> and the verb <ja>抱く</ja> means \"to hug\". This noun is similar, but it usually means carrying by hugging, so <vocabulary>holding in one's arms</vocabulary> or <vocabulary>carrying</vocabulary>. This is one that children use a lot!",
